Id: rlog002i
Severity: INFO
Category: logging
Check: check_remotelog
Fix: Forward the logs to a host of their own (rsyslog's omfwd, syslog-ng's tcp(), journal-upload).
References: rsyslog.conf(5); syslog-ng.conf(5)

No remote logging is configured: every log stays on this host. The
first thing an intruder does with root is silence the logs, and a
disk that dies takes its own account with it. On a machine nobody
depends on that is a choice; on a server it is a gap.
